# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 2, "Flags", and Appendix B, The dialect: `i` folds case by Unicode simple case folding (K, U+212A KELVIN SIGN, three bytes, folds with `k`; `ß` never matches `ss`); without `m`, `^` and `$` are the text's ends, with it also after and before each `\n`; without `s`, `.` is never `\n`; a flag group sets the flags to the end of its enclosing group, across `|`, and a scoped one only inside itself.
